---
import BookmarkCard from '../cards/BookmarkCard.astro';
import ButtonCard from '../cards/ButtonCard.astro';
import CalloutCard from '../cards/CalloutCard.astro';
import CodeCard from '../cards/CodeCard.astro';
import GalleryCard from '../cards/GalleryCard.astro';
import ImageCard from '../cards/ImageCard.astro';
import ProductCard from '../cards/ProductCard.astro';
import PullQuoteCard from '../cards/PullQuoteCard.astro';
import ToggleCard from '../cards/ToggleCard.astro';
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';

// Held in a variable so the braces survive Astro's template expressions.
const codeSample = `@theme {
  --color-bg: var(--mirror-bg);
  --color-surface: var(--mirror-surface);
  --color-accent: var(--mirror-accent);
}`;

const bodyClass = 'text-body leading-body text-pretty';
const codeChipClass = 'rounded-[4px] border border-border bg-surface-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.88em]';
---

<section class='pt-18'>
	<SectionHeading tight>07 — Rendered post content</SectionHeading>
	<p class='text-muted mb-10 font-mono text-xs'>
		Measure locked to 68ch. Ghost card types below map 1:1 to the editor's card set.
	</p>

	<article class='measure mx-auto'>
		<h2 class='font-display text-h2 tracking-heading leading-[1.2] font-medium'>Heading two sets the chapter</h2>

		<p class:list={['mt-5', bodyClass]}>
			Body copy is the product. Everything else in a publishing theme exists to get out of its way — which means the
			measure, the leading, and the space above a heading matter more than any flourish. This paragraph runs at
			<strong>19px</strong> with a <strong>1.72</strong> line height.
		</p>

		<p class:list={['mt-5', bodyClass]}>
			Links inside prose stay in the accent colour with a 1px underline offset by 3px, so descenders stay legible.
			Inline <code class={codeChipClass}>code</code> gets a tinted chip.
		</p>

		<h3 class='font-display text-h3 mt-11 leading-[1.28] font-medium'>Heading three</h3>
		<p class:list={['mt-4', bodyClass]}>
			Headings step down by a fixed ratio and inherit the display face, keeping the vertical rhythm intact even in a
			4,000-word essay.
		</p>

		<h4 class='font-ui text-h4 mt-8 leading-[1.35] font-semibold'>Heading four switches to the UI face</h4>
		<p class:list={['mt-3.5', bodyClass]}>
			A deliberate break: at this size the grotesque reads as a label rather than a title.
		</p>

		<ul class='text-body leading-body mt-[22px] flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6'>
			<li>Unordered lists keep the body measure</li>
			<li>Markers sit in the muted tone</li>
			<li>Nested items indent by one step</li>
		</ul>

		<blockquote class='border-accent mt-10 border-l-[3px] py-1 pl-[26px]'>
			<p class='font-body text-text text-[calc(var(--text-body)*1.06)] leading-[1.55] italic'>
				A theme is a promise about how much you respect the reader's attention.
			</p>
			<cite class='font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-3.5 block uppercase not-italic'>
				Blockquote · attribution
			</cite>
		</blockquote>

		<PullQuoteCard />

		<CodeCard code={codeSample} />

		<ImageCard
			label='image card · regular width'
			caption='Caption sits left, one step down, muted.'
			aspect='aspect-[3/2]'
		/>

		<ImageCard
			label='wide image · breaks the measure'
			caption='Wide card — measure + 2×88px.'
			aspect='aspect-[21/9]'
			width='wide'
		/>

		<BookmarkCard />

		<GalleryCard />

		<ButtonCard />

		<CalloutCard>
			Callout card — for editor's notes, corrections, and disclosures. Four accent variants ship with the theme.
		</CalloutCard>

		<ToggleCard>
			Yes — free, paid, and comped tiers, with paywall gates, tier badges, and a members dashboard. Alpine drives the
			disclosure; <code class='font-mono'>aria-expanded</code> and <code class='font-mono'>aria-controls</code>
			stay bound to state.
		</ToggleCard>

		<hr class='border-border my-14 border-0 border-t' />

		<ProductCard />
	</article>
</section>
